            "review_text": "hannahlovescheese\nBirmingham, United Kingdom25 contributions\n1\nWhat is 'rattan top'!?\nSep 2016 • Couples\nOn arriving here it seemed quite nice. The decor is good. We sat down and had some pickled vegetables put in front of us. The staff didn't speak English, and there were a few ingredients we were unsure of. We both had dishes with something called 'rattan top' in - this seemed to be some sort of vegetable, there was loads of it in each dish and it was incredibly bitter, I had to spit it out. Other than this, the food was quite bland, the beer was warm and the staff seemed to deliberately ignore us when we tried to get their attention. They also charged us for the pickled cabbage that we didn't ask for in the first place. Would not recommend.\nRead more\nWritten September 4, 2016",
            "rating": 5.0,
